{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>There.</b> קפוז is not like קפוד (Isaiah 14:23) but a different bird." "<b>And it hatches.</b> And it gives birth. Likewise והמליטה זכר (Isaiah 66:7)." "<b>And it breaks [open].</b> Its derivation is לבקוע, to cleave." "<b>It gathers.</b> Like קרא דגר (Jeremiah 17:11)." "<b>Kites.</b> A plural form, like הדיה (Deuteronomy 14:13)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:43.486075810Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}